            "id":"PaolaLaf-SouthEast",
            "embedId":"852529567",
            "artist":"Paola Laf",
            "date":"15/07/2020",
            "datecode":"20200715",
            "colourName":"South-East",
            "colourHex":"#e77ee7",
            "link":"https://soundcloud.com/chromamixes/chroma-mix-paola-laf-200703-2049",
            "description":"This mix is made of tracks I've been listening to during the past 3 months in the midst of a global pandemic. It's got some dark and melancholic undertones which I associate with a shade of lilac. It includes two popular K-pop songs and therefore I didn't feel confident about it as a whole. Not because I don't like these songs but for fear of what others may think. Making this mix made me think a lot about what \"good music\" and what \"bad music\" is, what's \"cool\" and what's \"not cool\", what's \"underground\" and what's \"mainstream\", what's \"niche\" and what's \"popular\", what's \"high culture\" and what's \"low culture\". It made me question these parameters according to which we tend to judge music and pick what we like and don't like. It made me wonder if those other artists whose music I picked would be annoyed to be in a mix next to a K-pop song. Nevertheless I think these tracks work well together, sonically and also thematically. I hope you will enjoy it.",
            "imageUrl":"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/colours-project.appspot.com/o/images%2FmixImages%2FSchermata%202020-05-08%20alle%2023.47.36.png?alt=media&token=518d9053-f61f-49ef-97a4-4c6ac9a72eca",
